Those skills were substantially rewritten in this repository (organic state inference, persisted
non-shrinking plans, evidence contract, contract-class enumeration, survivor-first mutation,
required properties, plan contribution sections, two-tier safety gates; go-testing was rewritten
around races, leaks, order dependence, fuzzing and deterministic time). The remaining skills
(agent-eval, breakcheck, contract-compat-testing, crash-and-process-testing,
dependency-legitimacy, docker-test-containers, exploit-testing, iac-safe-auditor,
implementation-theater, llm-eval-design, llm-redteam, messaging-eventdriven-testing,
python-testing-patterns, rag-audit-evaluator, real-run-validation, resilience-fault-injection,
silent-degradation, test-strategy-verifier) and all Go code are original to this repository.

tsp complements gentle-ai (https://github.com/gentleman-programming/gentle-ai); apart from the
go-testing skill definition attributed above, it does not include, modify, or replace any part of it.
